{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Tzelah, she too, gave birth.</b> Therefore <b>גם</b> is written of her, to say that she too — who was chosen for marital relations — she too gave birth, and the sterilizing potions she was given did not help her, because there is a body that does not accept the remedy, as stated in chapter HaMapelet. And the <b>גם</b> here is interpreted as 'too,' like its Targum. Why does Scripture list the trades of the sons of Cain? Because the earth was cursed on account of their ancestor, they abandoned his trade — which is working the earth — and took up other trades. [And the sister of Tuval Cain, Naamah — a twin]."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:59.508486824Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}